DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppmmaapp__qqeenntteerr() function accepts a linear array of _c_o_u_n_t pointers to
     wired pages _*_m, and enters each of these pages into the kernel virtual
     address (KVA) space, beginning at the address _s_v_a.  The pages are mapped
     non-executable, if possible.  (For example, non-PAE i386 has no capabil‐
     ity to map pages non-executable.)

     The ppmmaapp__qqrreemmoovvee() function tears out a mapping from the kernel virtual
     address space, beginning at _s_v_a and for _c_o_u_n_t pages.

IIMMPPLLEEMMEENNTTAATTIIOONN NNOOTTEESS
     The ppmmaapp__qqeenntteerr() function is intended for temporary mappings that do not
     require page modification or reference counting.  Old mappings are simply
     overwritten.  The pages _m_u_s_t be wired into physical memory.

     The corresponding ppmmaapp__qqrreemmoovvee() function is intended to remove such tem‐
     porary mappings.

